{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Queued a second successor for the leader-verification question that measures the exposure bound instead of deriving it from source: after each verification case the probe now waits, bounded by five lease timeouts, for the isolated leader to stop reporting itself as leader, recording the lease timeout and elapsed wait. Local construction feedback showed the leader becoming a follower after about one lease interval in both timer configurations (about 62 ms with the default 50 ms lease and about 1013 ms with the slowed 1000 ms lease), but that receipt is unread, so the account still states the bound as source-derived.\"}"}}
